  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "matins",
      "title": "Matins",
      "sourceHeading": "Matins",
      "pages": [
        60
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Opening Prayer",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "O my God, to sing praises worthy of thy greatness, open my mouth; grant me the holy fervor of the angels. Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn O splendor of the King of angels, grant that a holy and divine zeal may inspire us to sing thy praises. O fair eyes that caused this innocent stream to flow, enkindle in our hearts a languishing zeal.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Jesus was troubled in spirit and, deeply moved, he asked Martha and Mary, ”Where have you laid Lazarus?” They replied, ”Lord, come and see.” And Jesus wept at these words.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Rare are the marvels of wonders,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. To see water flow from a rock. But what makes these wonders unparalleled is that this rock is God himself.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Oration",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0008",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Oalmighty and merciful God, who willed that thine only Son should weep over Lazarus’s death as a testimony of his love and raise him from the grave to reveal the miraculous power of his divinity, grant us the grace, through thy Holy Spirit, to think ceaselessly upon thee and to pray with the tears of holy devotion. May these salutary waters cleanse us of all our sins and raise us from the grave of iniquity. We ask this through Jesus Christ, our Lord. Amen.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0009",
          "verification": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lauds",
      "title": "Lauds",
      "sourceHeading": "Lauds",
      "pages": [
        60
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn Miracle of holy love! This God who casts thunder and forms the joys of the day, weeps and groans upon the earth. Seeing Lazarus dead, his heart is moved, and he washes his sin with a stream of tears.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "O Lord, how sweet and tender is thy Spirit! To deliver thy friend from death’s grasp, thou didst pour tears of sweetness from thy loving heart.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. As waters flow from two fountains,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Let my eyes pour forth streams of tears. The love they hold within shall become the drink of Heaven.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Oration",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "May the outpouring of thy tears, O Lord, purify our hearts, and may the holy dew of thy weeping render our souls fertile. We ask this through Jesus Christ, our Lord. Amen.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            60
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              60
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "lauds-b0008",
          "verification": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prime",
      "title": "Prime",
      "sourceHeading": "Prime",
      "pages": [
        61
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn O Word, almighty and noble support of creation, why is thy heart faint under the blows of nature? No, cruel death, halt thy fury. Cease to be a spectacle of horror before his eyes.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Jesus, seeing Martha and Mary weeping, wept also. O holy tears of a chaste lover, filled with compassion for two grieving sisters, who weep for the loss of their brother and witness the resurrection of one whose death was known to all.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. O divine source of life,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Abundant fountain of clarity, grant that my soul, enslaved, may find liberty in thee.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Oration",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Omost gracious and tender Jesus, who wept not only for Lazarus but also for all the world and for me, a miserable sinner, grant me the grace to honour thy holy tears with such tender devotion that they may enkindle in my heart the sacred fire of perfect love. Let my eyes shed the saving waters of true contrition so that, being purified by water and fire, my soul may be refreshed and find its eternal home in thy kingdom, where there shall be no more tears or sighs, but where thou livest and reignest gloriously forever.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0008",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Amen.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "prime-b0009",
          "verification": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "terce",
      "title": "Terce",
      "sourceHeading": "Terce",
      "pages": [
        61
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn O living star, divine sun, splendor of the Father’s glory, cast thy gaze upon the excess of our misery. Through this overwhelming love that caused thee to weep, grant us the blessings for which we sigh.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "The King of men wept; the joy of angels became sorrowful. If God himself laments with such sadness, who would not weep seeing him weep, who would not groan seeing him groan?",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Let our eyes pour forth tears;",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Let us flow with fountains of weeping. In our deepest afflictions, no sweeter solace can we find.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Oration As at Prime.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sext",
      "title": "Sext",
      "sourceHeading": "Sext",
      "pages": [
        61,
        62
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn O sun of eternity, thou who formest this chaste light, which restores our original innocence, dispel by thy tears this mournful night that hides the joy thy love produces.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            61
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              61
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "They removed the stone that sealed the tomb, and Jesus wept. The one who had been bound was immediately loosed and, though dead, rose to life.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. O august and divine power,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. That causeth waters and oil to flow in abundance from the mere touch of thy hand.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "sext-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Oration As at Prime.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
