            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "No star is more charming than this precious liquid. The sun is adorned with less splendor than its miraculous beauty. Honey pales in sweetness compared to its taste, which captivates both the heart and soul.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "We adore this precious tear, shed with sorrow and lamentation by the gentle Jesus. The angel stored it in a small vessel with reverence, and Mary Magdalene left it as her legacy when she departed this world.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Thou who, with a mighty tear,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0006",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Cleanseth the sins of mortals, receive the innocent ardor that bows us at thy altars.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0007",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Oration",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0008",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "May the labor of thy only Son relieve us in our struggles amid the perils of this life. Grant, O Lord, that the sweet dew of his tears, which we now honour, may quench the fire of our concupiscence and enkindle in us the flames of a holier and more divine love. We ask this through Jesus Christ, our Lord. Amen.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "none-b0009",
          "verification": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vespers",
      "title": "Vespers",
      "sourceHeading": "Vespers",
      "pages": [
        62,
        63
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Hymn Sweet and delightful vessel, rare marvel of wonders, O tear, the virtue of thy water knows no equal. Having despoiled death of its spoils, break for our sake its harsh strength.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "vespers-b0001",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Through thy mercy, O Lord, draw near to me; come and subdue the insolence of those who oppose thy law. Glory be to thee, divine essence; glory to thee, adorable Trinity, who art the reward of immortality.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "vespers-b0002",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Ant.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "vespers-b0003",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "The Lord Jesus satisfied our hunger with the bread of his tears and quenched our thirst with the water of his weeping.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "vespers-b0004",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Tears flow from my visage,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              62
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "vespers-b0005",
          "verification": "pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. To intoxicate with their water. Yet their intoxication brings wisdom to those who drink of this stream.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            62
